## 11. RECONCILIATION MATRIX — every source item's canonical home (no-orphan proof)

### 11.1 Document A register (24 items) → canonical
1 MDL → TCF-INDEX-001 · 2 Sys Requirements → SYS-REQ-001 (D) · 3 Architecture DD → SYS-DES-001 (D) · 4 Facility ICD → SYS-ICD-001 · 5 Cabling ICD → SYS-ICD-002 · 6 DUT Fixture ICD → SYS-ICD-003 · 7 Schematics & Calcs → SYS-DD-001 · 8 Assembly Drawings → SYS-DD-002 · 9 PCB Package → SYS-DD-003 · 10 FPGA DD → SYS-DD-004 · 11 LabVIEW DD → SYS-DD-005 · 12 Protection Architecture → SYS-DD-006 · 13 FMEA → SYS-RISK-002 · 14 Risk Assessment → SYS-RISK-001 · 15 Compliance Matrix → SYS-COMP-002 · 16 Safety Document → SYS-SAF-010 · 17 Verification Plan → SYS-VER-001 · 18 Test Reports → SYS-VER-1xx · 19 Calibration Records → SYS-CAL-001 · 20 BOM → SYS-DD-007 · 21 As-Built Baseline → SYS-CFG-001 (absorbed) · 22 IFU/Safety Manual → SYS-MAN-001 · 23 Labelling Schedule → SYS-LAB-001 · 24 Gen-2 Checklist → SYS-NG-001.

### 11.2 Document B / XLSX tree (SEC/DOC items) → canonical
DOC-01-01 Equipment Description & Intended Use → SYS-SAF-001 · DOC-01-02 Environmental Spec Log → SYS-COMP-001 classification block (+ SYS-SAF-001 §environment) · DOC-01-03 Informal DoC → SYS-COMP-003 Statement of Compliance (title retired, §8) · DOC-02-01 Single-Line Power Diagram → SYS-DD-001 delta (extract/attach) + SYS-SAF-003 power tree · DOC-02-02 PE Bonding Record → SYS-SAF-003 §PE + SYS-VER-1xx (PE continuity test) · DOC-02-03 Creepage & Clearance Analysis → SYS-SAF-003 §isolation (+ SYS-COMP-002 evidence) · DOC-02-04 Overcurrent & Short-Circuit Log → SYS-SAF-003 power tree/fuse schedule + SYS-VER-1xx (short-circuit tests) · DOC-03-01 Weight/CoG Map → SYS-DD-002 delta + SYS-MECH-001 · DOC-03-02 Stability Test Reports → SYS-VER-1xx · DOC-03-03 Caster/Structural Log → SYS-MECH-001 (+ test if needed) · DOC-03-04 Flammability Matrix → SYS-MECH-001 §materials + SYS-CMP-001 rows + SYS-DD-003 delta · DOC-04-01 Component Ledger → SYS-CMP-001 · DOC-04-02 Datasheets/Certs → SYS-CMP-001 Class-R annex · DOC-05-01 Operations Manual → SYS-MAN-001 · DOC-05-02 Maintenance & Earth-Continuity Guide → SYS-MAN-002 · DOC-05-03 Warning Labels Layout → SYS-LAB-001 + SYS-DD-002 delta.

### 11.3 Document C SYS-set → canonical
SYS-SAF-001 + SYS-SAF-002 → merged SYS-SAF-001 (decision recorded §4.2) · SYS-CFG-001 → same · SYS-COMP-001/002/003 → same · SYS-RISK-001 → same (+ Protective Measures annex) · SYS-SAF-003/004 → same · SYS-VER-001 → same · SYS-SW-001 → same · SYS-EMC-001 → stub (conflict resolution §4.5, Q11) · SYS-CAB-001 → annex of SYS-ICD-002 · SYS-MECH-001 → same · SYS-LAB-001 → same · SYS-MAN-001/002 → same · SYS-GAP-001 → same · SYS-NG-REQ-001 → same · TCF-INDEX-001 → same · C's 17-folder layout → TCF-INDEX-001 physical structure.

### 11.4 Document D 18 branches → canonical (branches are content sections, not documents)
1 Scope & Boundary → SYS-SAF-001 · 2 System Description → SYS-DES-001 + SYS-SAF-003 (power tree/I-O) · 3 Clause Gap Review → SYS-COMP-002 · 4 Hazard Analysis → SYS-RISK-001 · 5 Safety Requirements → SYS-REQ-002 · 6 Protective Measures → SYS-RISK-001 Annex A · 7 Electrical Evidence → SYS-SAF-003 (+ SYS-VER-1xx) · 8 Mechanical Evidence → SYS-MECH-001 (+ tests) · 9 Wiring & I/O → SYS-ICD-002 (+ schedule annex) · 10 Control & Software → SYS-SW-001 (+ SYS-DD-004/005 deltas) · 11 Marking & Instructions → SYS-LAB-001 + SYS-MAN-001/002 · 12 Verification & Validation → SYS-VER-001 · 13 Test Records → SYS-VER-1xx · 14 File Structure → TCF-INDEX-001 · 15 Deviations & Rationale → SYS-GAP-001 (+ Safety Document §7.8) · 16 Change Impact → SYS-GAP-001 `NEXT-GEN` tags + SYS-NG-REQ-001 · 17 Compliance Wording → §8 of this spec + SYS-COMP-001/003 · 18 Next-Generation Seed → SYS-NG-REQ-001 + SYS-NG-001.

### 11.5 Recorded conflicts and their resolutions
| # | Conflict | Resolution (revisit trigger) |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | EMC in scope (C §12) vs out of scope (A §1) | A wins: out of scope; ≤2-pp position stub SYS-EMC-001; full EMC deferred to Gen-2 plan. (Q11) |
| R2 | Four competing trees/numbering schemes (A register, B SEC/DOC, C SYS-xxx, D 18 branches) | A's register is the document set; C's prefixes are the numbering; B/D items mapped as content/annexes per 11.2/11.4. (Q6) |
| R3 | B "Informal Declaration of Conformity" vs A's explicit non-CE stance | Retired; Statement of Compliance inside SYS-COMP-003. |
| R4 | C splits boundary/intended-use into two docs vs A Rule 1 anti-proliferation | Merged into one SYS-SAF-001. |
| R5 | Cable length ~25 m (A) vs "several m to 15 m+" (C) | Configuration-dependent; per-baseline record. (Q16) |
| R6 | B's clause numbers & numeric limits vs A §3's "confirm against held edition" | All provisional, `[confirm ref]`/`[confirm vs clause]` tags until Phase 4. (Q2, Q14) |
| R7 | Document proliferation risk: C generates ~20 docs, D implies 18 more | Canonical register caps controlled docs at ~31 by making C/D items sections and annexes per A Rules 1–2. |

